      "message": "per previous discussion, it\u0027s better to decide if a feature is enabled based on the specific module version, considering that if the module rollback happens and the boolean value might be overlaid (e.g. when module rolls back to a previous version, but the boolean value is still true, that will result in the feature is still enabled on the previous version, which might not be intended). So later we migrate the flag value to module integer from boolean, and determine if the feature is enabled or not based on the module version.\n\nProbably we could do similar things here. Maybe refer to the flag defined in the IpClientLinkObserver for the code refactor(something like: \nisNetlinkEventParsingEnabled() https://source.corp.google.com/android/packages/modules/NetworkStack/src/android/net/ip/IpClientLinkObserver.java;l\u003d218;rcl\u003dHEAD?q\u003dIpClientLinkOb\u0026ss\u003dpiper%2FGoogle%2Fandroid), which calls DeviceConfigUtils.isFeatureEnabled().",
